{%- doc -%}
  Render a list of prices for a product, variant or line item.

  @param {object} [product] - if provided, the prices are rendered for the whole product
  @param {object} [variant] - if provided, then only the price from this variant is rendered
  @param {object} [line_item] - if provided, then the price from this line item is rendered (used on cart or order)
  @param {boolean} [hide_unit_price] - if set to true unit prices are hidden (mostly useful for size constrained elements)
  @param {string} [context] - can be "product", "line_item" or "card". This controls how the prices are displayed
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Zaria: the struck original is written first and the selling price second, so a reduced price
  reads "was, now" from left to right (client, 2026-11-09). The couture product page and the
  Zaria product strips were already in that order; the cards and the cart line were the odd ones
  out. Each price keeps its own screen-reader label, so the order is only visual.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  case context
    when 'card', 'line_item'
      assign base_text_class = ''

      if settings.product_card_text_font == 'heading'
        assign base_text_class = 'h6 '
      endif

      assign regular_price_classes = base_text_class | append: 'text-subdued'
      assign on_sale_price_classes = base_text_class | append: 'text-on-sale'
      assign compare_at_price_classes = base_text_class | append: 'text-subdued line-through'
      assign unit_price_classes = base_text_class | append: 'text-subdued'

    when 'product'
      assign regular_price_classes = base_text_class | append: 'h4 text-subdued'
      assign on_sale_price_classes = base_text_class | append: 'h4 text-on-sale'
      assign compare_at_price_classes = base_text_class | append: 'h5 text-subdued line-through'
      assign unit_price_classes = base_text_class | append: 'h6 text-subdued'
  endcase

  comment
    Zaria: fabrics are sold by the metre, so show a "/ metre" unit next to the price.
    Scoped to products tagged "Fabric" (perfumes / ready-to-wear are untagged and unaffected),
    and only in browsing/PDP contexts (not the cart line item).
  endcomment
  assign uom_product = product
  if uom_product == blank and variant != blank
    assign uom_product = variant.product
  endif
  if uom_product == blank and line_item != blank
    assign uom_product = line_item.product
  endif
  comment
    Zaria: a Ramadan piece is priced as the making alone, with the cloth charged beside it by
    the metre, so a card reading the variant price told half the story (client, 2026-11-13).
    Each of those products carries custom.price_from - the making plus the least expensive
    bolt that can still cut it, written by zaria-ops/madetoorder-from-price.mjs - and the
    card and the strips show that as a "from" figure instead. A cart line is left alone: it
    prints the money actually charged, and by then the cloth is its own line anyway. The
    cloth's own pricing is untouched.
  endcomment
  assign mto_from = 0
  if uom_product.tags contains 'Ramadan 2027' and line_item == blank
    assign mto_from = uom_product.metafields.custom.price_from.value | plus: 0
  endif
  if settings.currency_code_enabled
    assign mto_money = mto_from | money_with_currency
  else
    assign mto_money = mto_from | money
  endif

  assign show_uom = false
  assign fabric_unit = false
  if uom_product.tags contains 'Fabric'
    comment
      Zaria: cloth is cut in half metres, so the sold unit is 0.5 m and the variant price is
      the price of half a metre (cart quantities cannot be fractions). Customers think in
      metres, so a fabric price is doubled back to the metre wherever it is shown. Line items
      are left alone: they print the money actually charged.
    endcomment
    assign fabric_unit = true
    assign show_uom = true
  endif
-%}

<price-list class="price-list {% if context == 'product' %}price-list--product{% endif %}">
  {%- liquid
    assign shown_price = variant.price
    assign shown_compare = variant.compare_at_price
    if fabric_unit
      assign shown_price = shown_price | times: 2
      assign shown_compare = shown_compare | times: 2
    endif
  -%}
  {%- if mto_from > 0 -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
      MADE TO ORDER CASE - the making plus the cheapest cloth that can cut it
      --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <sale-price class="{{ regular_price_classes }}">
      <span class="sr-only">{{ 'product.price.sale_price' | t }}</span>
      {{- 'product.price.from_price_html' | t: price_min: mto_money -}}
    </sale-price>
  {%- elsif variant != blank -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
      VARIANT CASE (used on product page, quick view...)
      --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if variant.compare_at_price > variant.price -%}
      <compare-at-price class="{{ compare_at_price_classes }}">
        <span class="sr-only">{{ 'product.price.regular_price' | t }}</span>

        {%- if settings.currency_code_enabled -%}
          {{- shown_compare | money_with_currency -}}
        {%- else -%}
          {{- shown_compare | money -}}
        {%- endif -%}
      </compare-at-price>
    {%- endif -%}

    <sale-price class="{% if variant.compare_at_price > variant.price %}{{ on_sale_price_classes }}{% else %}{{ regular_price_classes }}{% endif %}">
      <span class="sr-only">{{ 'product.price.sale_price' | t }}</span>

      {%- if settings.currency_code_enabled -%}
        {{- shown_price | money_with_currency -}}
      {%- else -%}
        {{- shown_price | money -}}
      {%- endif -%}
    </sale-price>
  {%- elsif line_item != blank -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
      LINE ITEM CASE (used on cart, order page...)
      --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign li_price = line_item.final_price
      assign li_original = line_item.original_price
      if fabric_unit
        assign li_price = li_price | times: 2
        assign li_original = li_original | times: 2
      endif
    -%}
    {%- if line_item.original_price > line_item.final_price -%}
      <compare-at-price class="{{ compare_at_price_classes }}">
        <span class="sr-only">{{ 'product.price.regular_price' | t }}</span>

        {%- if settings.currency_code_enabled -%}
          {{- li_original | money_with_currency -}}
        {%- else -%}
          {{- li_original | money -}}
        {%- endif -%}
      </compare-at-price>
    {%- endif -%}

    <sale-price class="{% if line_item.original_price > line_item.final_price %}{{ on_sale_price_classes }}{% else %}{{ regular_price_classes }}{% endif %}">
      <span class="sr-only">{{ 'product.price.sale_price' | t }}</span>

      {%- if settings.currency_code_enabled -%}
        {{- li_price | money_with_currency -}}
      {%- else -%}
        {{- li_price | money -}}
      {%- endif -%}
    </sale-price>
  {%- elsif product != blank -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
      PRODUCT CASE (used on card)
      --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- liquid
      if product.price_varies and settings.product_price_strategy != 'from_price'
        assign variant = product.variants | sort: 'price' | last | default: product.selected_or_first_available_variant
      else
        assign variant = product.variants | sort: 'price' | first | default: product.selected_or_first_available_variant
      endif

      assign card_price = variant.price
      assign card_compare_at_price = variant.compare_at_price
      if fabric_unit
        assign card_price = card_price | times: 2
        assign card_compare_at_price = card_compare_at_price | times: 2
      endif

      if settings.currency_code_enabled
        assign variant_price = card_price | money_with_currency
        assign variant_compare_at_price = card_compare_at_price | money_with_currency
      else
        assign variant_price = card_price | money
        assign variant_compare_at_price = card_compare_at_price | money
      endif
    -%}

    {%- if variant.price < variant.compare_at_price -%}
      <compare-at-price class="{{ compare_at_price_classes }}">
        <span class="sr-only">{{ 'product.price.regular_price' | t }}</span>
        {{- variant_compare_at_price -}}
      </compare-at-price>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if product.price_varies -%}
      {%- assign is_variant_on_sale = false -%}

      {%- if variant.price < variant.compare_at_price -%}
        {%- assign is_variant_on_sale = true -%}
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if settings.product_price_strategy == 'from_price' -%}
        <sale-price class="{% if is_variant_on_sale %}{{ on_sale_price_classes }}{% else %}{{ regular_price_classes }}{% endif %}">
          <span class="sr-only">{{ 'product.price.sale_price' | t }}</span>
          {{- 'product.price.from_price_html' | t: price_min: variant_price -}}
        </sale-price>
      {%- else -%}
        <sale-price class="{{ on_sale_price_classes }}">
          <span class="sr-only">{{ 'product.price.sale_price' | t }}</span>
          {{- variant_price -}}
        </sale-price>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- else -%}
      <sale-price class="{% if variant.price < variant.compare_at_price %}{{ on_sale_price_classes }}{% else %}{{ regular_price_classes }}{% endif %}">
        <span class="sr-only">{{ 'product.price.sale_price' | t }}</span>
        {{- variant_price -}}
      </sale-price>
    {%- endif -%}

  {%- else -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
      PLACEHOLDER CASE (used on featured product section for instance)
      --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    {%- endcomment -%}

    <sale-price class="{{ regular_price_classes }}">
      <span class="sr-only">{{ 'product.price.sale_price' | t }}</span>

      {%- if settings.currency_code_enabled -%}
        {{- 4999 | money_with_currency -}}
      {%- else -%}
        {{- 4999 | money -}}
      {%- endif -%}
    </sale-price>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if show_uom -%}
    <span class="price-uom text-subdued" style="font-size:1em;margin-inline-start:.4em;letter-spacing:.02em;white-space:nowrap;">/ metre</span>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- unless hide_unit_price -%}
    {%- assign item = variant | default: line_item | default: product.selected_or_first_available_variant -%}

    {%- if item.unit_price -%}
      <unit-price class="{{ unit_price_classes }}">
        (
        {{- item.unit_price | unit_price_with_measurement: item.unit_price_measurement -}}
        )
      </unit-price>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endunless -%}
</price-list>
